---
// Meet Lauren — magazine feature (big display name, multi-column article,
// full-height cutout right). Copy: "About Lauren" from Copy Updates_Sept
// 2026 (Celestine's doc, swapped in Sep 1), verbatim — main story then the
// career paragraphs. Cutout: TEMPORARY — Lauren is sending a new photo
// that includes her children; swap it in when it lands.
---

<section class="fc-lauren-d" id="meet-lauren" aria-labelledby="lauren-title-d" data-nav-cream>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="article">
      <h2 id="lauren-title-d" data-rv style="--rvi: 0">Meet Lauren Kassan</h2>

      <p class="dek" data-rv style="--rvi: 1">
        Founder and CEO of STAND
      </p>

      <div class="cols" data-rv style="--rvi: 2">
        <p>
          Lauren learned by doing. Getting it right, getting it wrong, trying
          again. That made her more capable than any classroom could have.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now a mother of two, she thinks a lot about what kids need. Schools
          do a lot well, but the world is changing faster than any classroom
          can keep up with. She wants to help kids think for themselves, solve
          real problems, talk without a screen between them, gain financial
          literacy before it can scare them, and carry an idea all the way to
          the end.
        </p>
        <p>
          That&rsquo;s what she&rsquo;s building with STAND. Entrepreneurship
          is the vehicle. Everything they learn along the way is the point.
        </p>
        <p>
          This fall STAND opens its first location in Los Angeles, for kids
          ages 8-to-13. The modern-day lemonade stand for the next
          generation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/enroll" class="signup-line">Sign up here</a> to join us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lauren has spent her career building things from scratch. She was
          the first employee at SLT, led business development at ClassPass,
          and co-founded The Wing. She&rsquo;s been named to Forbes 30 Under
          30, Fast Company&rsquo;s 100 Most Creative People in Business, and
          Goldman Sachs&rsquo; 100 Most Intriguing Entrepreneurs.
        </p>
        <p>
          She never went to business school. She just did business. Now
          she&rsquo;s building the place she wishes existed when she was a
          kid figuring it out on her own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <img
      class="cutout"
      src="/brand/lauren-cutout-2.webp"
      alt="Lauren, founder and CEO of STAND"
      loading="lazy"
      width="427"
      height="749"
      data-rv
      style="--rvi: 3"
    />
  </div>
</section>

